.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_INTEGER_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_INTEGER_new ,
.Nm ASN1_INTEGER_free
.Nd ASN1_INTEGER allocation functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo ASN1_INTEGER_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ASN1_INTEGER_free
.Fa "ASN1_INTEGER *a"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ASN1_INTEGER_new
returns an allocated
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_INTEGER_free
frees up a single
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
object.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure representing the ASN.1 INTEGER type
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ASN1_INTEGER_new
return a valid
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_INTEGER_free
does not return a value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
